From: local-patch <local@invalid>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 16:40:45 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] edged: report pod sources ready only after kubelet
 processed the initial pods

The kubeedge kubernetes fork (a2eaf54ed8) made PodConfig.SeenAllSources
return initPodReady only, which edged sets right after queueing the pod
list. While kubelet's syncLoop skips pod updates (runtime/PLEG not yet
healthy) the volume populator then finishes with an empty pod manager and
the reconciler tears down volumes of running pods. Restore the upstream
seenSources check (kubelet processed an update from every source, every
source sent its first SET) on top of initPodReady, and defer pod messages
received before the initial list so the first apiserver-source update is
the initial SET.
